# 0028 XeGfx core: compressed scanout BOs, IOSurface import by surface, GEM mmap ceiling fix, hang diagnostics
#
# Base:  gpu/ after 0001 + 0008 + 0011 + 0020 + 0022 + 0023
# Files: gpu/xegfx/shim/include/{xg_fd.h, xg_i915.h, xg_vm_xnu.h, xg_xnu.h},
#        gpu/xegfx/shim/src/fbsd/{xg_fd.c, xg_kern.c, xg_lock.c, xg_mem.c, xg_misc.c, xg_vm.c},
#        gpu/xegfx/shim/src/xnu/{xg_fd.cpp, xg_kext.cpp, xg_vm.cpp},
#        gpu/xkpi/src/i915/{xg_display_hook.c, xg_i915_flip.c, xg_i915_map.c}; new: gpu/xkpi/include/linux/io.h
# Apply: patch -p1 < patches/0028-core-ccs-scanout-surface-import-mmap.patch
# Build: core 7f4f344c9e19 (link / kpi / shadow checks pass; installed with tools/install-m3d.py --core, reboot)
#
# Compressed scanout (docs/render-compression.md):
#   - XG_DRM_IOCTL_BO_SCANOUT / BO_UNSCANOUT ('N' 0x48 / 0x49, xg_i915_map.c): the XeMTL plugin names one of its own
#     GEM objects (a Tile4 + MTL RC CCS image: pixels, then the CCS at 1/256) on its DRM file; the core pins its pages
#     and hands back a token.  The pages stay pinned until the plugin lets go or the file closes.  The token, not the
#     handle, crosses into the accel, so a stale one finds nothing instead of another process's object.
#   - resident call "xgScanoutPhys" (token, phys[], cap, {pages, bytes}): every 4 KiB page of that object, the way
#     xgFlipMap takes them, so the accel can point a flip slot at the compressed image itself.
#   - resident call "xgPlaneLayout2" / xg_display_kms_plane_layout2(): a third plane layout, 2 = Tile4 with render
#     compression (I915_FORMAT_MOD_4_TILED_MTL_RC_CCS), plane 1 = the packed CCS at the given offset and pitch from
#     each frame's start.  The CCS pitch must be main pitch / 512 * 64 and the offset 4 KiB aligned past the main
#     surface, or the commit is refused.  The boot placeholder has no room for a CCS, so this layout commits its own
#     shmem placeholder (zero CCS = uncompressed), made on first use and grown when a larger one is asked for, so the
#     PLANE_AUX_DIST i915 programs holds for every image the accel then flips to.  The old two-layout entry
#     (xg_display_kms_plane_layout, 0 linear / 1 Tile4) stays and calls the new one.
#
# Import by surface:
#   - an IOSurface WindowServer imports is made from the surface's own kernel memory instead of a userptr that pins
#     its user mapping page by page (~2 us a page on the first execbuffer, most of it the shim's vm_page records).
#     ANV cannot import a GEM handle through our fds (it sizes a dma-buf with lseek, and the libdrm stand-in's fds are
#     pipes), so the plugin keeps its host-pointer import and announces it:
#       1. the accel looks the surface up in the caller's task and calls "xgSurfTicket" (descriptor, task): the core
#          retains the IOMemoryDescriptor and returns a one-shot ticket bound to that task;
#       2. the plugin names the ticket with the pointer and size it is about to import, XG_DRM_IOCTL_SURF_EXPECT
#          ('N' 0x4A) on ANV's own DRM file;
#       3. the matching DRM_IOCTL_I915_GEM_USERPTR on that file (now routed through the map hook: xg_fd.c) gets an
#          object whose pages are the descriptor's physical ranges, wired once with prepare().  Like a stolen object
#          it has no struct pages, only DMA addresses: no CPU write domain, the LLC-coherent caching a userptr gets.
#          The descriptor is completed and released with the object.  A plain userptr goes on to i915 as before.
#     Tickets and announcements nobody matched expire after 2 s or go with their file.
#   - xg_vm.cpp: xg_md_retain / xg_md_drop / xg_md_length / xg_md_prepare_ranges (wire, merged physical ranges) and
#     xg_current_task for the above.
#   - debug.xegfx_uhold: userptr page holds (count, pages, prepare / physseg / per-page run time, unwire) and the
#     imports by surface (imports, pages, ranges, ns per page, freed, live, failed).
#
# GEM mmap ceiling (the plugin's second descriptor pool failed with VK_ERROR_MEMORY_MAP_FAILED, ~1 s stall each):
#   - xg_map_ranges() and the surface import kept two arrays of one entry per page from kcalloc().  LinuxKPI's kmalloc
#     above a page is contigmalloc, which is IOMallocContiguous here and fails once XNU's free memory fragments: a
#     64 MB map needed two 128 KB physically contiguous blocks, so the largest mmap fell from 152 MB after boot to
#     48-64 MB after some hours.  Both now use kvcalloc / kvfree (virtually contiguous).
#   - xg_mem.c: contigmalloc failures are counted (debug.xegfx_mem: "contig fails N (largest S)"), the first eight
#     logged with their size, to find any other kmalloc above a page that still depends on contiguous memory.
#
# Hang diagnostics (an occasional hang where one CPU no longer answers the debugger's NMI):
#   - each CPU's irq-off watchdog slot also records its thread and three callers (frame-pointer walk limited to the
#     current 4 KiB stack page), the spin mutex it waits for and that lock's owner (xg_lock.c), and a register read
#     still in flight: the overlay gpu/xkpi/include/linux/io.h wraps readl / readq in xg_mmio_begin / xg_mmio_end, and
#     resident call "xgMmioHooks" lets the accel record its own display register reads (who = 2).
#   - the watchdog's panic string lists every CPU with interrupts off, a spin mutex, or an MMIO read older than 1 ms,
#     the owner's CPU, and the read as an offset into i915's MMIO window (xg_mmio_regs_base).
#
# Smaller changes:
#   - xg_fd.c: WindowServer may raise its GPU context priority (PRIV_SCHED_SETPRIORITY is granted to the compositor
#     only), so the GuC runs composites ahead of the apps' batches.
#   - xg_misc.c: firmware requests time out after 2 s instead of 30 s; a DMC image that is not embedded held the GuC
#     load behind it for 3 x 30 s at boot.
#   - xg_fd.cpp: the whole execbuffer (nr 0x69) is timed at the ioctl entry for the existing execbuffer statistics.
#
# Verified: after the reboot WindowServer opened its second descriptor pool without a single "mmap failed" or
# vkCreateDescriptorPool error, debug.xegfx_mem showed "contig fails 0", and compressed scanout and surface imports ran
# as before (debug.xegfxaccel_iop_xe_ccs_frames, debug.xegfx_uhold).
#
